            <ArticleTitle>Acute ischaemic colitis; a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">Acute ischaemic colitis (AIC) is being increasingly recognised as an uncommon cause of abdominal pain associated with fresh bleeding per rectum. It is paramount to maintain a high index of suspicion and adopt appropriate management strategies to avoid complications and inappropriate interventions. In this paper, we describe a case of AIC and review literature pertinent to the management of this condition.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="KEYWORDS" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Ischaemic colitis, acute abdomen, management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
